# Row Level Security (RLS)

## Schema

- Every table that stores user data must include `user_id` (UUID, FK to `auth.users`).
- Enable RLS on those tables; do not rely on client filtering alone.

## Policies (intent)

- `SELECT` / `UPDATE` / `DELETE`: only when `auth.uid() = user_id`.
- `INSERT`: require `user_id = auth.uid()` (or set it from the session server-side).
- Prefer the anon/authenticated roles with RLS over bypassing via `service_role` in app code.

## App code

- Always scope queries to the authenticated user; still assume RLS is the real boundary.
- Never disable RLS in production migrations without an explicit security review note.
